+/// The adapter this configuration asks for (step `mailer/1.19-test-layering`).
+///
+/// The choice is made in exactly one place, and every handler is written against the port — which is
+/// what step `mailer/1.13-email-port` bought: adding a real transport cost this function and nothing
+/// else. No host configured means the logging adapter, on purpose: it is what every earlier step's
+/// tests run against, and a service that refused to start without a mail server could not be tested
+/// on a laptop.
+fn adapter(config: &Config) -> Arc<dyn EmailSender> {
+    match &config.email.smtp_host {
+        // 25 is the port a mail server is expected to listen on; a test container is where the
+        // default is wrong, and that is exactly why the port is a setting.
+        Some(host) => Arc::new(Smtp::new(host, config.email.smtp_port.unwrap_or(25))),
+        None => Arc::new(Logging),
+    }
+}
